{"name":"Sassafras","hex":"#5a3940","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sassafras","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Lauraceae – sassafras trees."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Shoalhaven council area, eastern New South Wales, Australia.","A locality in Latrobe council area and the Meander Valley council area, northern Tasmania, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sassafras"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sassafras","blocks":[{"text":"Sassafras is a genus of three extant and one extinct species of deciduous trees in the family Lauraceae, native to eastern North America and eastern Asia. The genus is distinguished by its aromatic properties, which have made the tree useful to humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sassafras_Leaves_June_Nbg_%28261691941%29.jpeg/330px-Sassafras_Leaves_June_Nbg_%28261691941%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sassafras","wikidata":"Q131532"},{"title":"Sassafras (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Sassafras are a rock band from South Wales first formed in 1970. They play a mix of rock and roll, progressive rock and country rock with the emphasis on vocal harmony. The use of twin guitar solos, played by original members Dai Shell and Ralph Evans, continues to be a distinctive feature of their music. The band holds the UK record for the group performing the greatest number of live gigs in a year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Sassafras_at_the_Earl_Haig.jpg/330px-Sassafras_at_the_Earl_Haig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sassafras_(band)","wikidata":"Q20685447"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Sassafras_albidum%2C_Sassafras_pistillate_flowers%2C_Howard_Cou